note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note Control for unroll-write-i.om: contract section 4 line 89 restricts only unrolled bodies, and an
note OM-2 unit keeps the OM-1 meaning of everything not stated (lines 5-6). OM-1 accepts a write to the
note counter of a rolled for (observed under 734f0a39, twin unroll-write-i-rolled-om1.om); the counter
note is then advanced by the for's increment (OMEGESE 9.8 continue: "the increment of a for, so the
note counter still advances"). Expected stdout 1 and 3: oracle/s3s4/exp/unroll-write-i-rolled.out.
om2
fn main to int
for i ulong 4
i = add i 1
pu i
end
ret 0
end
